## Conclusion

A wedding day's sound is not one setup, it is several, run by the same technician from the first guest to the last dance: a soundcheck, a wireless handheld microphone for the vows and the speeches, a reset between your ceremony and reception spaces if they differ, and a volume shift into dancing. [Contact us](/contact/) to talk through your ceremony and reception. For our complete audio visual rental range in Malaga, see the [audio visual rental](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) guide.

## FAQs

### What microphone do you use for the vows, and who holds it?

One of the wireless handheld microphones included in the Wedding Pack, held by the officiant, so neither of you has to stand near a microphone stand during your vows. If the officiant needs both hands free, a wireless lavalier is available as a separate, quote based item. See [During the Vows](#during-the-vows-the-officiants-microphone-and-why-it-needs-a-technician) above.

### Why does a lavalier microphone need a technician present?

A lavalier microphone, worn close to the body and run through a live PA system, is genuinely more prone to feedback than a handheld microphone. If you add one for the officiant, the technician the Wedding Pack includes for the full event watches for that risk and adjusts before your guests notice. See [During the Vows](#during-the-vows-the-officiants-microphone-and-why-it-needs-a-technician) above.

### What happens to the sound setup between the ceremony and the reception?

Our technician already adjusts sound continuously as your day moves from ceremony to speeches to dancing. When that also means a change of room, the same room by room principle applies: a space's acoustics change what correct settings look like, which is exactly why the Wedding Pack technician has no hour cap. See [The Ceremony to Reception Switch](#the-ceremony-to-reception-switch-when-your-venue-changes-mid-event) above.

### Is there a soundcheck before the ceremony starts?

Yes. Our crew tests the officiant's microphone and the ceremony speakers against the actual venue before your first guest is seated, not hours earlier in an empty room. See [Before the Ceremony](#before-the-ceremony-soundcheck-and-setup) above.

### Does the technician stay for speeches and dancing too, or just the ceremony?

The whole event, with no hour cap, the only package in our catalog built that way. The same technician manages the wireless microphones from the vows through the speeches, then brings the volume up for dancing later in the night. See [Speeches at the Reception](#speeches-at-the-reception-the-handheld-microphone-and-the-handoff) and [Dancing](#dancing-when-the-volume-changes) above.
